  "notes": "{寝|ね}そべる is an intransitive godan verb. It emphasizes a relaxed, sprawled-out posture — not sleeping, but lying down idly.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{寝|ね}そべっている describes someone currently lying sprawled out.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～に{寝|ね}そべる (to sprawl on a surface)\n- ～で{寝|ね}そべる (to lounge around in a place)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ソファーに{寝|ね}そべる (to sprawl on the sofa)\n- {床|ゆか}に{寝|ね}そべる (to sprawl on the floor)\n- {芝生|しばふ}に{寝|ね}そべる (to lie on the grass)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n{横|よこ}になる is a neutral way to say \"to lie down.\" {寝|ね}そべる adds the nuance of doing so lazily or casually, often with limbs spread out.",
